Package: incomeLato
Title: Relative Income Position for 'Latinobarometro' Respondents from a
    Frozen Imputation Model
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Pedro", "Barbosa", email = "mrbarbosa.pedro@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Applies a frozen multinomial model (version 'v1.5') that
    predicts each respondent's relative income position within their
    country and survey year -- the probabilities of belonging to the
    bottom 50 percent, the middle 40 percent and the top 10 percent -- to
    'Latinobarometro' microdata that the user downloads from the official
    source. The model was trained on national household surveys and
    validated against 'LAPOP AmericasBarometer' data for 15 Latin American
    countries. It uses five predictors (sex, age, education, car
    ownership, washing machine ownership) plus a country effect, and the
    package harmonizes them across waves 1995-2024 through a manually
    curated crosswalk. The package ships only model parameters and
    variable-name metadata: it contains no survey microdata and no
    statistics computed from it. Probabilities are meant as continuous
    weights for aggregate analysis, not for classifying individuals.
